    "text": "Consider the system of equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math>, then the sum of all possible distinct value(s) of <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> for which system does not possess a unique solution is"
